{
  "slug": "daily-temperatures",
  "title": "Waiting for Warmer Days",
  "topic": "stack",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "pattern": "stack / Next greater",
  "statement": "# Daily Temperatures\n\nGiven an array `temperatures` where `temperatures[i]` is the temperature of day `i`, compute for every day how many days pass before a strictly warmer temperature occurs. When no future day is warmer, record `0` for that day.\n\nReturn an array of the same length holding one waiting time per day.\n\nConstraints: `1 <= temperatures.length <= 100` and `30 <= temperatures[i] <= 100`.\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "temperatures = [95, 60, 65]",
      "output": "[0, 1, 0]",
      "explanation": "Day 0 (95) has no future warmer day (0). Day 1 (60) sees warmer temperature 65 on day 2 (wait of 1 day). Day 2 (65) is the last day (0)."
    },
    {
      "input": "temperatures = [58, 30, 39, 37, 59, 38, 34, 72]",
      "output": "[4, 1, 2, 1, 3, 2, 1, 0]",
      "explanation": "For 58 at index 0, the next warmer temperature is 59 at index 4 (wait of 4 days). For 30 at index 1, the next warmer is 39 at index 2 (wait of 1 day)."
    },
    {
      "input": "temperatures = [30]",
      "output": "[0]",
      "explanation": "With only one day in the record, no subsequent warmer day exists, so the wait is 0."
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "Function signature: `function dailyTemperatures(temperatures: number[])`.",
    "Inputs are JSON-serializable values satisfying the bounds stated above."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Keep unresolved day indices on a decreasing stack.",
    "When a warmer day arrives, pop every cooler day it resolves.",
    "Leave unanswered days at zero."
  ],
  "editorial": {
    "approach": "Walk days forward, keeping indices with unanswered waits on a decreasing stack.",
    "why_optimal": "Each index is pushed and popped at most once, so the scan is linear with a stack bounded by the input.",
    "pitfalls": "Record zero for days with no warmer future day; never default to the end of the array."
  },
  "reading_links": [
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stack_(abstract_data_type)"
  ],
